     "value": "VREF, 12 V"
    },
    {
     "ref": "J4",
     "type": "terminal",
     "value": "15 V supply"
    }
   ],
   "notes": [
    "Design targets: 15V supply, 12V reference, 2V to 10V in, ±8V differential out.",
    "Resistors of 6 kΩ or less keep their noise under the amplifier noise where noise matters.",
    "Swept over 0 V to 12 V of input, the outputs leave their straight line near both ends; 2 V to 10 V is the range used.",
    "With a 10 MHz bandwidth figure for the NE5532, the circuit is limited to signals under 10 MHz."
   ]
  },
